    <!-- Unit Overview -->
    <section class="welcome-section">
        <h2><i class="fa-solid fa-compass section-icon"></i> Unit Overview</h2>
        <p>The focus is on Synthesis and Strategic Justification. HL students must go beyond understanding the emerging technology to evaluating it within a global, multi-layered framework. Key themes include Operational Constraints (e.g., latency, battery life), Scalability, and the Interplay of Conflicting Factors (e.g., efficiency vs. privacy).</p>
    </section>

    <!-- Syllabus Links -->
    <section class="content-section">
        <h2><i class="fa-solid fa-bookmark section-icon"></i> What You'll Learn</h2>
        <div class="learning-points">
            <ul>
                <li>
                    Deep Research: Investigating the four challenge questions (2 SL + 2 HL-specific).
                </li>
                <li>
                    Technical Synthesis: Linking research papers and white papers to the core technical concepts of the syllabus (A1, A2, A3, A4, B3, B4).
                </li>
                <li>
                    Strategy Formulation: Drafting and justifying comprehensive strategies for the case study organisation (e.g., "BotPro").
                </li>
                <li>
                    Real-world Context: Mapping theoretical research to documented real-world deployments and expert findings (e.g., vSLAM in fire rescue).
                </li>
            </ul>
        </div>
    </section>

